## WY Riot Control Team

cmu-wyriot-name-leader = WY Riot Control Team Leader
cmu-wyriot-description-leader = Lead a PMC Dispatch riot control team. Break up the crowd, protect Company property and bring the ringleaders in alive.
cmu-wyriot-prefix-leader = RCT. TL.
cmu-wyriot-name-specialist = WY Crowd Control Specialist
cmu-wyriot-description-specialist = A PMC Dispatch crowd control specialist. Beanbags, batons and tear gas: the Company wants its property back and its colonists quiet, not dead.
cmu-wyriot-prefix-specialist = RCT.
cmu-wyriot-supervisors-leader = The riot control team leader
cmu-wyriot-name-grenadier = WY Crowd Control Grenadier
cmu-wyriot-description-grenadier = A PMC Dispatch crowd control specialist with an M81 riot launcher. Break up the crowd from a distance with tear gas and flashbangs.
cmu-wyriot-greeting = You are a Weyland-Yutani riot control contractor, sent in by PMC Dispatch because colonists have turned on Company property. Restore order with non-lethal force, protect Company staff and property, and hand the ringleaders to the Corporate Liaison.
cmu-wyriot-rules = You are a WY riot control contractor. Use non-lethal force against unarmed rioters. Lethal force is for those who are armed and show intent to use it.

## WY Corporate Security Team

cmu-wysecteam-name-sergeant = WY Security Team Sergeant
cmu-wysecteam-description-sergeant = Lead a Corporate Security detail sent to reinforce a Company site. Report to the site's senior employee and put your officers where the site needs them.
cmu-wysecteam-name-officer = WY Security Team Officer
cmu-wysecteam-description-officer = A Corporate Security officer sent to reinforce a Company site. Protect Company staff, property and research.
cmu-wysecteam-greeting = You are Weyland-Yutani Corporate Security, sent to reinforce a Company site. Report to the senior employee on site, follow your Sergeant, and protect the Company's people, property and research.
cmu-wysecteam-rules = You are Weyland-Yutani Corporate Security reinforcing a Company site. Follow the senior employee on site and your Sergeant, and use proportionate force.
